{"id": "EUVD-2026-86839", "enisaUuid": "c1cc2e62-1bd4-3b47-b452-02eb044fa2d5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Skip vport under deletion in report ID acquisition\n\nqla24xx_report_id_acquisition() format-1 handling walks ha->vp_list under\nvport_slock, takes a vref_count on the matching vport and calls\nqla_update_host_map() to register its port id.\n\nA vport teardown via qla24xx_vport_delete() sets VPORT_DELETE, then\nqla24xx_disable_vp() removes the vport from the host_map btree and zeroes\nvha->d_id (RESET_AL_PA). The vport is only unlinked from vp_list later,\nin qla24xx_deallocate_vp_id(), which clears vp_map[idx] (RESET_VP_IDX)\nbut does not touch host_map. In the window in between, report ID\nacquisition can still find the vport on vp_list and call\nqla_update_host_map(); with d_id already zeroed it takes the\nbtree_insert32() path and re-inserts the dying vport into host_map.\nNothing cleans that entry afterwards, so once scsi_host_put() frees the\nvha a later host_map lookup dereferences freed memory.\n\nSkip a vport that has VPORT_DELETE set before taking the reference, so it\nis neither re-registered nor scheduled for DPC re-registration. This\nmirrors the existing guard in qla2x00_alert_all_vps().", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:07", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40dcd4a71a52414b47fbba2f956387f1077c6c15", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20bb54601d2655e83795b73499c89f6b1cb31016", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d61e8de98c5a52978fb1edd95fe4dde3131b280e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a83979d92782f83c90888ebe19bdc9420521940", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23582731afa35031c94fadb71a4f3b4afd094649"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pr28-3mcx-gcmr", "CVE-2026-97531"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "58df61e3-4238-3202-9596-4ccd29eefdfc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "41dc529a4602ac737020f423f84686a81de38e6d <40dcd4a71a52414b47fbba2f956387f1077c6c15"}, {"id": "5fe1afce-6e0f-3d8c-aa2f-0d16f27fd90c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.11"}, {"id": "6a383e9a-afa3-3604-8444-e1677a4d2b01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "705f17a7-02f1-343d-937d-77129f3158ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "9936951c-2763-3b13-8092-31372d6a2530", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "41dc529a4602ac737020f423f84686a81de38e6d <20bb54601d2655e83795b73499c89f6b1cb31016"}, {"id": "9f74549a-7d2e-35e8-808a-cb449b76a52b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "a8c55d79-8233-3545-9e39-c912b4fe395a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "41dc529a4602ac737020f423f84686a81de38e6d <23582731afa35031c94fadb71a4f3b4afd094649"}, {"id": "a9355a8e-33ca-3a53-9ee5-5ea9114973b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a94f8f2b-158c-3028-a8b6-bc2de82d3d3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "b246108d-1181-3533-8e77-44842cdca671", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "fe79e48d-6c72-3c63-b9ae-e3d45ee6ed0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "41dc529a4602ac737020f423f84686a81de38e6d <d61e8de98c5a52978fb1edd95fe4dde3131b280e"}, {"id": "fefe7436-a8ea-3ad5-a6ca-a275db12dd5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "41dc529a4602ac737020f423f84686a81de38e6d <7